<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Open the agent workspace</h3>

<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-list--spaced">
  <li>From the Connect admin home (the page you reached via "Log in for emergency access" in step 1), open the <strong>top-right account dropdown</strong> and click <strong>Agent Workspace</strong>. It opens in a new tab.</li>
  <li>Confirm you can see the Contact Control Panel (CCP) on the left, the Customer Profile and Cases tabs in the middle, and the Connect assistant pane on the right.</li>
  <li>Click the <strong>Apps</strong> dropdown at the top of the workspace. Among "Performance metrics" and "Worklist" you should see the bespoke <strong>NDX:Try Aldershire</strong> app, which gives you a branded dashboard with caller lookup and quick links.</li>
</ol>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Mark yourself Available</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">In the CCP on the left, the status drop-down at the top probably says "Offline". Click it and choose <strong>Available</strong>. The chip turns green. You are now in the routing pool for inbound contacts.</p>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Take the call</h3>

<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-list--spaced">
  <li>Pick up your <strong>mobile phone</strong> (or any phone that isn't the laptop running the workspace).</li>
  <li>Dial the <code>PstnNumber</code> from step 1.</li>
  <li>Say something with sustained distress in it. The script from step 6 works well, or just speak in character: <em>"I don't know what to do, my neighbour's been threatening me and the council won't return my calls and I'm scared to leave the house."</em></li>
  <li>Watch the agent workspace. Within seconds, an incoming-call popup appears with caller phone, intent guess, and a sentiment chip.</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Accept</strong>. The live transcript starts streaming. Sentiment chips on each segment colour green to amber to red as the conversation unfolds.</li>
  <li>The Cases tab in the middle updates: <code>safeguarding_flag: true</code> appears with a red badge once distress is sustained.</li>
</ol>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">What to look for</h3>

<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li><strong>The Connect assistant pane on the right</strong> &mdash; Q in Connect surfaces relevant Knowledge Base articles automatically. As soon as the caller mentions safeguarding, "Aldershire DC safeguarding contacts and escalation" pops to the top.</li>
  <li><strong>The caller lookup form</strong> in the bespoke NDX:Try app &mdash; type the caller's phone, get back any open cases, recent contacts, and the Customer Profile.</li>
  <li><strong>The redacted transcript</strong> &mdash; the caller's name and address appear as <code>{NAME}</code> and <code>{ADDRESS}</code> placeholders, even in your live agent view. Contact Lens redacts at instance level; there is no path that exposes the original PII to the agent.</li>
</ul>

<p class="govuk-body">When the caller hangs up (or you wrap up), Connect Cases keeps the ticket. The safeguarding flag means it surfaces in the safeguarding queue's daily review, not in the general triage.</p>
